From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:22:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build(deps): drop the stale google-antigravity cooldown
 exemption

uv.toml exempted google-antigravity from the 7-day dependency cooldown
with a fixed `exclude-newer-package` date (2026-06-12) so the then-new
SDK could resolve. A fixed date also excludes every later release, so
uv.lock stayed on 0.1.2 while PyPI moved on. The package is well past
the cooldown, so remove the exemption as its comment asked and re-lock
with `uv lock --upgrade-package google-antigravity`, which picks
0.1.23 (the newest release older than 7 days). No other locked
package changes: 0.1.23's new `protobuf>=7.35` floor is already met by
the locked protobuf 7.35.1.

0.1.23 no longer fills `Step.usage_metadata` (it is deprecated, and
usage now arrives as conversation-level updates), so the antigravity
executor would report no token usage for a turn. After the step stream
ends, read `conversation.last_turn_usage`, which both 0.1.2 and 0.1.23
expose as the per-turn total, and keep the per-step value as a
fallback. The rest of the SDK surface the executor uses is unchanged.

Upstream pull request: https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/14704.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/antigravity-cooldown; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (dependency re-lock and a token-usage fix in the antigravity harness; no setting)
---
 omnigent/inner/antigravity_executor.py   |  9 ++++-
 tests/inner/test_antigravity_executor.py | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 uv.lock                                  | 14 +++----
 uv.toml                                  |  5 +--
 4 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/omnigent/inner/antigravity_executor.py b/omnigent/inner/antigravity_executor.py
index 5b76d3f47fd92aa7a1e7abf1896399c93166c40c..d747d8e8a713d5de1e545d2fc83b31ab0e007b41 100644
--- a/omnigent/inner/antigravity_executor.py
+++ b/omnigent/inner/antigravity_executor.py
@@ -19,7 +19,9 @@ Streaming model:
 
 - ``agent.conversation.receive_steps()`` yields :class:`Step` objects as the
   turn runs (``content_delta``, ``thinking_delta``, ``tool_calls``,
-  ``status``, ``usage_metadata``), ending once the turn goes idle. A producer
+  ``status``), ending once the turn goes idle. Token usage comes from
+  ``conversation.last_turn_usage``, or ``Step.usage_metadata`` on SDKs that
+  still set it. A producer
   task drives ``send()`` + ``receive_steps()`` and feeds a per-turn
   :class:`asyncio.Queue`; :meth:`run_turn` drains it and yields mapped events.
 - Tool *requests* derive from ``Step.tool_calls`` (deduped by call id); tool
@@ -647,6 +649,11 @@ class AntigravityExecutor(Executor):
                     )
                     queue.put_nowait(ExecutorError(message=message, retryable=(status == "ERROR")))
                     return
+            # Newer SDKs leave ``Step.usage_metadata`` unset and track usage on
+            # the conversation, so prefer its per-turn total when it exposes one.
+            turn_usage = getattr(conversation, "last_turn_usage", None)
+            if turn_usage is not None:
+                state.last_usage = turn_usage
         except asyncio.CancelledError:
             # Consumer teardown; conversation.cancel() already requested by
             # interrupt_session, nothing to emit.
diff --git a/tests/inner/test_antigravity_executor.py b/tests/inner/test_antigravity_executor.py
